      <workList xml:id="workDesc_c32c38c5">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e219216">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_93f8878e">A4:501</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_eb359253" xml:lang="it">Quadro I a flauto, 2 violini e basso</title>
            <title xml:id="title_fde25e28" xml:lang="it">Partita III a flauto obl., 2 violini e basso</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_669346a3">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_5e30af03">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_2b384c89">
               <p xml:id="idm114">The present work for a flute, two violins and bass, is listed twice in one of Breitkopf's catalogues (1765); it has since been lost. The composition appears as the first in a collection of two 'Quadri da diversi [autori]' of which the second one is by <persName xml:id="idm115" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Malzart</persName>. The same work also appears as the third in a collection of six 'Partite da diversi autori' (raccolta 6) which includes works by <persName xml:id="idm116" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Moecke</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm117" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Schürer</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm118" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Reichardt</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm119" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Trier</persName> and <persName xml:id="idm120" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Werner</persName>. It is likely that the work was composed before Scheibe's arrival in Copenhagen in 1740.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_0e5f6a37">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
            </langUsage>
